---
Audited in a fresh `cp -a` copy at scratch/x8/budget2 (kept .git; the first
attempt at this copy was a stale leftover from a prior session and was
discarded/redone before any conclusions were drawn from it).

## Summary

Attempt 2's own, narrowly-scoped fix (the 12 sites in kpis.html /
guardrails.html that attempt 1 FAILed) is CORRECT, COMPLETE, and introduces
no regressions — verified independently below. But a live-render sweep of
the rest of task X8's own manifest surfaced the *same defect class*,
introduced by the *same X8 sweep*, at roughly 9x the scale (106 more sites
across 26 more files) that attempt 1's own audit did not catch and attempt 2
was never asked to fix. Since it is squarely X8's own replicated content
(not pre-existing baggage — see attribution below) and directly fails
ACCESSIBILITY.md points 7/12 (WCAG 1.4.3 AA), the task as a whole cannot be
accepted yet, so this pass is a FAIL despite attempt 2 doing its assigned
job correctly.

## 1. Independent contrast recomputation for the 12 sites attempt 1 FAILed (own math, not trusting the claim)

Colors pulled straight from the shipped `web/static/css/tailwind.css`
(`grep -o '\.dark\\:text-gray-400[^{]*{[^}]*}' ...` etc.):
- `dark:text-gray-400` = rgb(156,163,175); `dark:text-gray-500` =
  rgb(107,114,128); `dark:bg-gray-800` (solid) = rgb(31,41,55); body
  `bg-gray-900` = rgb(17,24,39) (`web/templates/layouts/base.html:57`);
  `dark:bg-rose-900/20` = rgba(136,19,55,.2); `dark:bg-red-900/20` =
  rgba(127,29,29,.2); `dark:bg-green-900/20` = rgba(20,83,45,.2).

Compositing sanity check (read the templates, not assumed): kpis.html's
rose card (`bg-rose-50 dark:bg-rose-900/20`, line 101) is a top-level grid
item, so it composites over the page body `bg-gray-900` — confirmed.
guardrails.html's red/green boxes (lines 18, 38) are nested *inside* the
parent `bg-white dark:bg-gray-800` card (line 3), so they composite over
`gray-800`, not the body — confirmed by reading the template structure.

Using WCAG relative-luminance formula (own Python, sRGB->linear, standard
weights), with dark:text-gray-500 (the *pre-fix* color) reproduces attempt
1's own FAIL numbers exactly: gray-800 solid 3.04:1, rose-900/20-over-body
3.48:1, red-900/20-nested 2.96:1, green-900/20-nested 2.80:1 — confirms my
compositing model matches the one attempt 1 used.

With dark:text-gray-400 (attempt 2's fix), the same 4 surfaces:
  gray-800 solid card (kpis.html:60,77,81,141,150,159,179,185;
    guardrails.html:6,72,89,114,120)        -> 5.78:1
  rose-900/20 over body (kpis.html:111,113)  -> 6.62:1
  red-900/20 nested in gray-800 (guardrails floor box, 22,26,29,33) -> 5.64:1
  green-900/20 nested in gray-800 (guardrails ceiling box, 42,46,49,53) -> 5.34:1
All 12 sites clear 4.5:1 (they're text-xs/text-sm/text-[10px], no large-text
carve-out applies). Matches attempt 2's claimed 5.34-6.62:1 range.

## 2. Delta discipline

`grep -n 'dark:text-gray-500' web/templates/components/kpis.html
web/templates/components/whatif/guardrails.html` -> zero hits in both files.
`git diff master` for the two files (206-line diff, read in full) shows
every hunk accounted for: the 12 dark-token swaps (500->400) with light
halves left exactly as attempt 1's own quoted before/after (e.g. "text-
gray-400 dark:text-gray-500 (master) -> text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-500
(X8) at line 111" in the X8.1 verdict matches current line 111 verbatim
except for the dark token, which is the only change attempt 2 made there),
plus attempt-1-authored, already-reviewed content (h3->h2 heading
promotions consistent with the whatif-page heading audit, text-green-600
->text-green-700 consistent with attempt 1's own PASS section, other
light-side gray-400->500/600 sweep edits). No attempt-2 changes exist
outside the 12 dark tokens.

## 3. No new dark-mode regressions on the same cards (≥4 samples, own computation)

  kpis 2xl value dark:text-gray-100 on gray-800 solid card         -> 13.34:1
  kpis 2xl value dark:text-gray-100 on rose-900/20-over-body card  -> 15.27:1
  guardrails h2 dark:text-gray-100 on gray-800 card                -> 13.34:1
  guardrails Floor label dark:text-red-300 on red-900/20 nested    ->  7.54:1
  guardrails Ceiling label dark:text-green-300 on green-900/20     ->  9.65:1
  guardrails event row dark:text-red-400 on red-900/20 nested      ->  5.17:1
  guardrails event row dark:text-green-400 on green-900/20 nested  ->  7.78:1
All clear. No regression introduced by the 12-token fix.

