## 6. Real render + axe (not template source, not guessed CSS)

Built and ran `cmd/server` against an empty `BUDGET_DATA_DIR` (200 OK,
empty-state render, confirmed via server log). Curled `/dashboard` and
`/whatif`, wrapped each in light and `class="dark"` HTML documents loading
the actual shipped `web/static/css/tailwind.css`, ran
`npx @axe-core/cli ... --tags wcag2a,wcag2aa,wcag21a,wcag21aa,wcag22aa`
against all 4 pages. None of axe's reported `color-contrast` violation
selectors reference anything from kpis.html or guardrails.html (confirmed
by grepping the full axe output for guardrail/floor/ceiling/kpi terms —
zero hits) — the 12-site fix is clean in a real render, not just in theory.
Heading check on the live `whatif` render: 1 h1, all-h2 sections in
sequence including "Drop/rise guardrails (simple)" (now h2, promoted from
h3 by attempt 1's earlier work) fits correctly with no skipped level.

Remaining axe hits on these 4 pages (chart-placeholder color-contrast x5,
label x9, select-name x6) are all in files/elements untouched by X8.2 and
most predate X8 entirely (`git diff master -- <file>` shows the specific
placeholder lines byte-identical to master, e.g. the chart-loading divs on
dashboard.html); reported as OBSERVATION, not attributed to this attempt.

## 7. FAIL — ACCESSIBILITY.md points 7 & 12 (WCAG 1.4.3 AA), site-wide, attributable to X8's own sweep

While confirming "attempt 1's clean audit of the other 52 files still
stands" (verify step 4), a live-render/grep sweep for the *same* defect
pattern attempt 1 found (light-mode caption color swept up, paired
`dark:text-gray-500` caption color left behind) turned up 110 more
occurrences of `dark:text-gray-500` outside kpis.html/guardrails.html,
across 26 files:

  `grep -rc 'dark:text-gray-500' web/templates/` -> 110 occurrences / 28 files
  (kpis.html and guardrails.html are 2 of the 28, now clean; the other 26
  files still have it)

Attribution (git diff master, per-line, not per-file): wrote a script that,
for every line containing `dark:text-gray-500`, checks whether that exact
line existed verbatim anywhere in `git show master:<file>`. Result: **106
of 110 lines do NOT exist in master** — i.e. these lines were edited by
X8's own sweep (the light-mode class was changed on the same line, e.g.
`text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500` (master) -> `text-gray-500
dark:text-gray-500` (current) in
`web/templates/components/whatif/rate-assumptions.html:106` and 40+ other
lines in that one file alone). This is the *identical* pattern — same root
cause, same mechanism — that attempt 1 itself ruled was not "inherited
baggage the sweep walked past" but "the sweep's own... decision," and
FAILed on in kpis.html/guardrails.html. Only 4 of 110 lines are genuinely
untouched (byte-identical to a master line) and are properly PRE-EXISTING/
OBSERVATION.

All 28 affected files are in X8's own `.swarm/manifests/X8.1.files`
manifest — this is not out-of-scope content:
  `comm -12 <(files with dark:text-gray-500) <(sort X8.1.files)` -> 28 of 28.

Compositing verified by direct template read for two more samples (in
addition to the 12 already-fixed sites): `budget-vs-actual.html:13` and
`whatif/income-chart.html:25` both sit in a top-level `bg-white
dark:bg-gray-800` solid card, same background as the fixed kpis/guardrails
solid-card sites. Contrast recomputed with the same script as #1:
`dark:text-gray-500` (rgb(107,114,128)) on `dark:bg-gray-800`
(rgb(31,41,55)) = **3.04:1** — fails 4.5:1 for the text-xs/text-[10px]
captions ("Loading chart...", "No data", "Recently Removed",
"Simulation parameters", etc — the overwhelming majority of the 106
sites); a handful of text-2xl font-bold instances (e.g.
`insights.html:189` "$0.00") clear the 3:1 large-text floor at 3.04:1 but
that is a razor's-edge pass on a value the constitution would still flag
under point 12 (dark parity — light-mode gray-500 on white is nowhere near
this close to its own floor).

Representative sites (file:line, all still `dark:text-gray-500`, all
verified via template read to sit on a `dark:bg-gray-800` or darker
composited surface, all text-xs/text-sm/text-[10px] unless noted):
  budget-vs-actual.html:13,18 (chart loading / empty-state captions)
  whatif/income-chart.html:25 (chart loading caption)
  whatif/projection-chart.html:36 (chart loading caption)
  whatif/monte-carlo.html:104,105,140,145,150,155 (simulation detail captions)
  whatif/rate-assumptions.html: 18 sites (helper text under every rate input)
  whatif/budget-analysis.html: 12 sites (tax/withdrawal breakdown captions)
  whatif/social-security.html, whatif/roth-conversion.html,
  whatif/portfolio-settings.html, whatif/rmd.html, whatif/tax-summary.html,
  whatif/present-value.html, whatif/healthcare-person.html,
  whatif/income-sources-list.html, whatif/expense-sources-list.html,
  whatif/bigticket-card.html, whatif/onetime-card.html,
  whatif/scenario-chain-card.html, whatif/conversion-sweep.html,
  whatif/projection-breakdown.html, whatif/tax-optimizer.html,
  pages/dashboard.html, pages/insights.html, pages/major-expenses.html,
  pages/transfers.html, pages/filemanager.html, pages/unlock.html,
  pages/explorer.html — each carries multiple instances (full per-line list
  reproducible via the attribution script above; omitted here for length).

This is a real, currently-shipping WCAG 1.4.3 AA failure at a scale ~9x
larger than the one attempt 1 caught, self-inflicted by X8's own contrast
sweep, still present after attempt 2. Attempt 2 did exactly what its
manifest asked (kpis.html + guardrails.html only) and did it correctly —
that piece is not in question — but the task cannot be marked accepted
while its own sweep leaves ~100+ AA-failing caption instances live across
26 other files it already touched. This needs to go back to a worker
(full-file sweep of `dark:text-gray-500` -> `dark:text-gray-400` mirroring
the fix just verified, with a fresh completeness check that greps for the
literal token pattern rather than spot-checking specific colors) before
re-verification.

## Observations (non-blocking)

- Attempt 1's "Sweep completeness" section (point 3 of its verdict) checked
  only `grep -rn 'text-green-600'`; it did not run the equivalent grep for
  `dark:text-gray-500`, which is why this scale of the same defect class
  went uncaught. Worth tightening the checker's own completeness-check
  methodology for future sweeps, not just re-running it here.
- monte-carlo.html:268 decorative svg still lacks `aria-hidden="true"`;
  byte-identical to master both before and after this attempt, pre-existing,
  out of scope.
- axe's 5 chart-placeholder color-contrast hits, 9 `label` hits, and 6
  `select-name` hits on dashboard/whatif are all in files/lines
  byte-identical to master (`git diff master` confirms per-file) — genuine
  pre-existing defects, not attributable to X8, reported for the lead's
  backlog only.
